import os, sys
out = sys.argv[1]
head = '''You are making game art for "Pause" (Unity, vertical 2D shooter, phone portrait, the player flies UP the screen). Work ONLY inside this directory tree; do not edit any .cs/.meta/.json or any existing file; do not delete anything; do not commit.
New files go ONLY to ./Pause/Assets/Art/Resources/ShipArt/Dove/src~/codex/ (the trailing ~ matters: Unity ignores it). Put helpers in its tools/ subfolder.
Read ./docs/art-style.md first (neon pixel art). The player ship is "Dove", redrawn in hi-res neon pixel art (aqua-teal egg-shaped body, light cyan hex canopy, red slit lights, white-and-red diamond wingtip lights, gunmetal tail pod with amber nozzle lip).

REFERENCES (attached images, in order): (1) skinref_state0.png, (2) skinref_state1.png, (3) skinref_state2.png: the FINAL approved flipbook, three 3 x 3 sheets (intact, damaged, wreck), 9 poses each in the order key pose / bob up / bob up lights off / glint 1 / glint 2 lights off / bob down / bank left / bank right / hit flash. Each is 1536 x 1536 (cells 512 px).
RULES: no pink or magenta anywhere. No flames. No outline or halo around the ship. Flat pure #00FF00 background.
'''
body = '''
JOB SKIN-{name}: a COLOURWAY of the finished flipbook. Redraw each of the three sheets in the "{name}" colourway and write skin_{name}_state0.png, skin_{name}_state1.png, skin_{name}_state2.png (same 3 x 3 layout, each cell 1024 x 1024 i.e. 3072 x 3072 per file, flat #00FF00 background, every pose at the SAME position and scale as the reference sheet). THE DRAWING MUST STAY IDENTICAL cell for cell (same silhouette, panel lines, damage, cracks, glints, bank shape, light dashes): ONLY COLOURS CHANGE:
{rules}
Everything else (canopy glass, tail pod and nozzle glow, glints, and ALL damage effects: blown panels, sparks, glowing orange tears, embers, soot) stays as in the reference, in the same places on the same panels in every cell. The hit-flash cell stays bone-white. Do not add new damage and do not remove any.
Use IMAGE GENERATION to repaint each sheet from the reference (several candidates, pick the truest to the reference), then clean with nearest-neighbour. Do NOT simply hue-shift with a script: the result must be a painted redraw with new ramp shading, but pixel-faithful to the drawing (same plating texture, panel lines and rim lights, in the new colours).
Write tools/check_skin_{name}.py that, for each of the three files and each of the 9 cells, prints: silhouette (non-green mask) difference vs the reference cell (must be < 1.5%), difference over the canopy region (must be < 6%), and the fraction of all pixels that changed (must be > {chg}% so it is visibly a new colourway). FIX AND REDRAW until every number passes; print the summary in your final message. Finish with honest caveats.
'''
skins = {
    'Night': ('''- the aqua-teal ARMOUR (all teal plating with its darker shading and light highlights) becomes deep midnight indigo-navy metal: base #2A2E6B, shadow #1A1F45, rim-light highlights bright cyan #6EF2EE along the upper-left edges of the plates (neon edge lighting) and a few pale blue-white highlights. Keep the canopy glass, the red slit lights and the wingtip diamonds as they are.''', 12),
    'Sodium': ('''- the aqua-teal ARMOUR becomes warm sodium-lamp ORANGE metal: base #F2862B, shadow #A9481A, highlights #FFB43C with pale yellow-white hot edges. Keep the canopy glass, the red slit lights and the wingtip diamonds as they are.''', 12),
    'Bone': ('''- the aqua-teal ARMOUR becomes warm BONE-white ceramic armour: base #F4EAD4, shadow #B9AE98, highlights near-white, with plate seams in a slightly darker warm grey. The canopy stays cyan; the red slit lights and wingtip diamonds stay red/white so they still read.''', 12),
    'Courier': ('''- this is the special SPLIT livery with a CLEAN left/right division, no mottling: split the hull exactly down the centre spine line (the vertical axis through the nose, canopy and tail): the LEFT half of the ship (as seen in the picture, including the left wing stub and left half of the tail pod) keeps the aqua-teal armour exactly as in the reference; the whole RIGHT half (right wing stub, right flank, right half of the nose/body plating, down to the tail) becomes warm bone-white ceramic armour: base #F4EAD4, shadow #B9AE98, highlights near-white, with the same plate seams and rim lights. The division is a single straight vertical line at the spine from the tip of the nose to the tail, the canopy glass stays cyan across both halves, the red slit lights and wingtip diamonds stay. In the bank poses the division follows the spine line of the banked hull. Damage panels and scorch on either side stay exactly as they are (cavities stay dark, just the surrounding armour takes its half's colour).''', 3),
}
for k, (rules, chg) in skins.items():
    open(os.path.join(out, 'skin_%s.md' % k), 'w').write(head + body.format(name=k, rules=rules, chg=chg))
